From ae8c42086005b479a5316afcd54a6ef2b5c1a15d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 09:31:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] update-pause cancel keeps the cancelled call's own
 result below the stamp

The mid-tool core-update cancel replaced every cancelled call's result with
the bare stamp. On 2026-11-13 07:08:31Z that dropped run_in_user_terminal's
{"error":"interrupted","job_id":"20261112-230727-c18e35"}; the resumed turn
polled with the wrong id and a Terraform apply's outcome was lost
(t_01a1d40fc0dda5c3).

update_pause_cancel.committed now appends the call's own text result below
the stamp (with_own_result: head 1536 + tail 512 chars, so a job_id at the
start or a session_id at the end survives), closed by an end line so a kept
"[Command interrupted]" tail is not rewritten away by replay cleanup. The
executor's own "[Tool execution cancelled/skipped -" text and empty or
non-text results still get the bare stamp.

The stamp wording changes from "re-run if still needed" to "check its outcome
before re-running" (both the Desktop pause and the Kanban restart
continuation), so a side-effecting call is not re-run blindly.

Kanban: t_01a1d41fd158579d
